From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erik Bourget <address-in-upstream-commit@localhost>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 02:29:04 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 44/93] drm/apple: publish completion of native display
 takeover

A display controller the bootloader left scanning out a framebuffer can
still show that surface after DRM registration. Reserve its retirement
record with the cache controller when binding, and mark it retired
once an accepted, shown KMS swap replaces or clears slot zero. A
paired firmware-27 scanout passes the firmware's shown state to the
owner, set when both engines displayed the retired swap. If the record
cannot be allocated the display still takes over, without a
retirement report, so allocation stays off.
Until that displayed completion arrives, pull the primary plane into
atomic commits for that CRTC so cursor- or overlay-only commits replay
the intended slot-zero surface with its own framebuffer reference,
force an explicit slot-zero clear when the primary plane is disabled,
and drop any inherited slot-zero reference from the pending scanout to
match that clear.

Signed-off-by: Erik Bourget <address-in-upstream-commit@localhost>
